I don't know if this bug has been documented before, but here it is:

My bold level 2 wizard decided to take on a shopkeeper.  So, I got into
the shop, put on a ring of invisibility, then started force bolting the
shopkeeper.  I ran out of energy, and picked up some throwing stars
from his shop and started throwing them at him.  He responded with the
usual "you are a thief!" line, but then instead of coming and attacking
me, he walked away, after which I got something like "no resident
shopkeeper" after throwing another star out of the shop, then a
"program in disorder" message.

I tried it again in wizard mode but couldn't reproduce it.

It seems to me that it probably doesn't know what to do when you throw
something out of a shop whose shopkeeper is alive but absent.



